  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "material",
      "summary": "The purchase-money anti-deficiency classification incorrectly limited the qualifying third-party purchase-loan category to institutional lenders, although current CCP 580b(a)(3) applies to a qualifying loan from a lender without that institutional restriction.",
      "resolution": "With root approval, changed the chapter paragraph and financing-rule-purchase-money-protection-classification rule and example to third-party lender wording with an explicit non-institutional qualifier. Renamed the related figure title; root independently re-reviewed and recorded that separate visual. The final rule digest here covers the corrected version."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": "Independent AI primary-source review, not qualified human legal or tax review, comprehensive case-law research, psychometric validation, or assurance of exam results. USDA direct-loan fact-sheet and guaranteed-program support was verified through indexed passages on the exact official sources because direct requests returned a maintenance portal or 403; no complete USDA PDF read is claimed. DRE reference-book and traditional CalVet material is used for identified structural or historical explanations; current statutes and regulations control. Review covers the rule records and read chapter bodies, not a new independent certification of all embedded visuals or linked practice questions; those have separate records. Body hashes are descriptive snapshots in scope, not machine-validated body artifacts under the current review schema."
}
